---
import JournalArticle from '../../components/JournalArticle.astro';
const title='Dither Boil: an AI-built tool for restless images';
const description='Shubham Shinde designed Dither Boil from a concept prompt; AI built the personalised browser tool for turning images and video clips into animated 1-bit dither loops.';
const poster='assets/journal/diwali/dither-poster.jpg';
const shareImage='assets/experiments/dither-archer-hero.jpg';
---
<JournalArticle section="experiments" slug="dither-tool" title={title} description={description} shareImage={shareImage} shareAlt="An archer drawing his bow, rendered in glowing white particles against a starry sky" projectUrl="/experiments/dither-boil/" readTime="1 min read" projectLabel="Try Dither Boil in your browser" keywords={['AI-assisted creative coding','dither animation tool','creative coding','image to animation','designer builder India']}>
  <figure class="journal-window"><a href="/experiments/dither-boil/" aria-label="Open the tool"><img src="/assets/experiments/dither-boil-ui-ember.jpg" alt="The Dither Boil interface: an archer boiling as glowing orange grain in the preview, with Presets, Pattern and Tone panels on the right" width="2400" height="1500" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></a><figcaption>Dither Boil running in the browser.</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="journal-copy">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p><strong>Dither Boil</strong> is a browser tool that turns any image or short video clip into animated 1-bit grain, then exports it as a still or a looping video.</p>
    <p>I wrote the concept prompt and AI built the tool. The effect runs live in your browser; nothing is generated, it transforms the file you give it.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol class="journal-steps">
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 16V4M7 9l5-5 5 5M4 16v4h16v-4"/></svg><div><b>Drop in a file</b><span>Any image or a short video clip.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/></svg><div><b>Pick a preset</b><span>Boil, Ordered, Diffusion or Hard cut.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h10M18 7h2M4 17h4M12 17h8"/><circle cx="16" cy="7" r="2"/><circle cx="10" cy="17" r="2"/></svg><div><b>Shape the grain</b><span>Dot size, grain, contrast, glow and the colour pair.</span></div></li>
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v12M7 11l5 5 5-5M4 20h16"/></svg><div><b>Export</b><span>A PNG still or a looping video.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</JournalArticle>
